<odoo noupdate="1">

    <record id="channel_bookings" model="slide.channel">
        <field name="name">Bookings: From Request to Gig Day</field>
        <field name="channel_type">training</field>
        <field name="description" type="html"><p>Take a booking request to a signed, paid, never-double-booked gig, and walk into the day with everything on one sheet.</p></field>
        <field name="visibility">members</field>
        <field name="enroll">invite</field>
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="enroll_group_ids" eval="[(6, 0, [ref('sales_team.group_sale_salesman')])]" />
    </record>
    <record id="channel_bookings_s1" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_bookings" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Requests and quotes</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">10</field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_bookings_s1_l1" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_bookings" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">The Book a Date form</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">11</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>Clients ask for a date on your website's <span class="oe-path">Book a Date</span> page (<code>/book</code>): their name and contact, the type of event, the date, start and end times, the venue, the number of guests and anything you should know.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/performers_elearning/static/img/book_form.png" alt="The Book a Date form on the website" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>the Book a Date page.</p></div><p>Each request becomes a lead in <span class="oe-path">CRM</span>, named after the gig, with all of that on its <strong>Gig</strong> details. Add the page to your website menu once, and it's protected from spam like any other Odoo form.</p><div class="oe-callout"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-clock-o" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">Times past midnight</span><p>An end time earlier than the start means the gig runs past midnight: 21:00 to 01:00 is a four-hour gig.</p></div></div><div class="oe-callout"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-building-o" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">More than one business?</span><p>Choose where this website's requests go in <span class="oe-path">Website › Configuration › Settings</span>, <strong>Booking Requests Go To</strong>. The lead and its quote belong to that team's company, so they use that company's settings and agreement terms.</p></div></div></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_bookings_s1_l2" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_bookings" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Packages and quotes</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">12</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>From the lead, <span class="oe-path">New Quotation</span> starts a quote with the gig's details already on its <strong>Gig</strong> tab. Pick a quote template for the package, and add-ons from its optional products.</p><p>Packages priced by the hour bill the gig's own length. On the product's <span class="oe-path">Gigs</span> tab, tick <strong>Bill the Gig's Hours</strong>: a 17:00 to 23:00 gig puts 6 hours on the quote, and changing the gig's times changes the hours while it's still a quote. A <strong>Minimum Hours</strong> setting in <span class="oe-path">Sales › Configuration › Settings</span> keeps short gigs from billing less.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/performers_elearning/static/img/quote_lines.png" alt="A quote with an hourly package at six hours and a PA rental" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>an hourly package at the gig's 6 hours, and a flat-priced PA rental.</p></div><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/performers_elearning/static/img/product_gigs_tab.png" alt="A product's Gigs tab" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>a package's <strong>Gigs</strong> tab: hourly billing, a to-do when booked, and its gear.</p></div><div class="oe-callout"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-check-square-o" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">A to-do when booked</span><p><strong>To-do When Booked</strong> on a product becomes a to-do for the salesperson the moment a gig with it is booked: for example, "Get the venue's equipment list" for a sound engineer working on house gear.</p></div></div></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_bookings_s1_l3" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_bookings" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Never booked twice</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">13</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>Every quote is checked against your confirmed gigs, your appearances and your own events, with a gap around each (set as <strong>Gap Between Gigs</strong> in Settings, 2 hours by default) for setup, travel and pack-down. Anything too close shows at the top of the quote.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/performers_elearning/static/img/double_booking.png" alt="A quote warning that the date is already booked" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>a quote that clashes with a gig already booked that night.</p></div><p>Confirming a clashing quote is stopped; if you really mean it (two short sets, say), use <strong>Confirm Anyway</strong>. <span class="oe-path">Sales › Orders › Booked Dates</span> shows every booked gig and event on a calendar.</p></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_bookings_s2" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_bookings" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Booked: signature, deposit and balance</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">23</field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_bookings_s2_l1" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_bookings" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Signature and deposit</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">24</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>Send the quote from Odoo. With <strong>Online Signature</strong> and <strong>Online Payment</strong> on (Settings, with the deposit as a percentage), the client signs and pays the deposit from the link, and that books the date: the quote becomes a sales order.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><div class="oe-flow"><div class="oe-flow-step"><span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-paper-plane" /></span>Send the quote</div><span class="oe-flow-arrow"><i class="fa fa-long-arrow-right" /></span><div class="oe-flow-step"><span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-pencil" /></span>Client signs</div><span class="oe-flow-arrow"><i class="fa fa-long-arrow-right" /></span><div class="oe-flow-step"><span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-credit-card" /></span>Pays the deposit</div><span class="oe-flow-arrow"><i class="fa fa-long-arrow-right" /></span><div class="oe-flow-step"><span class="oe-flow-step-icon"><i class="fa fa-calendar-check-o" /></span>Date booked</div></div></div><div class="oe-callout"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-bell" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">The balance</span><p>A daily job adds an <strong>Invoice the balance</strong> to-do on each booked gig coming up within <strong>Invoice Balance Before</strong> days (Settings, 14 by default).</p></div></div></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_bookings_s3" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_bookings" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">On the day</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">34</field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_bookings_s3_l1" model="slide.slide">
