        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">The timeline</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">35</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>The quote's <strong>Timeline</strong> tab holds the moments of the event: grand entrance, first dance, toasts, last song. Times after midnight sort after the evening.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/performers_elearning/static/img/timeline_tab.png" alt="A gig's timeline" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>a wedding's timeline.</p></div><p>Clients add to it themselves from their order in the customer portal (<strong>Your event timeline</strong>) until the gig starts; their moments are marked <strong>From Client</strong>.</p></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_bookings_s3_l2" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_bookings" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">The Gig Sheet</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">36</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>The <strong>Gig</strong> tab also takes the load-in time, the on-site contact and load-in notes (parking, stairs, power, curfew). <span class="oe-path">Print › Gig Sheet</span> puts the whole day on paper: the booking, times, venue, contacts, what was booked, the timeline, the notes and the gear checklist, with the song request card as its last page.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/performers_elearning/static/img/gig_sheet.png" alt="The Gig Sheet" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>the start of a Gig Sheet.</p></div></div></field>
    </record>
