    <record id="channel_gear_music" model="slide.channel">
        <field name="name">Gear and Music</field>
        <field name="channel_type">training</field>
        <field name="description" type="html"><p>Pack the right gear for every gig, and handle the client's music lists and guests' song requests.</p></field>
        <field name="visibility">members</field>
        <field name="enroll">invite</field>
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="enroll_group_ids" eval="[(6, 0, [ref('sales_team.group_sale_salesman')])]" />
    </record>
    <record id="channel_gear_music_s1" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_gear_music" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Gear</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">10</field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_gear_music_s1_l1" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_gear_music" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Your gear and each package's</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">11</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>List your gear once in <span class="oe-path">Sales › Configuration › Gear</span>: speakers, lights, mics, cables, and how many of each you own. Then, on each package or add-on, its <span class="oe-path">Gigs</span> tab lists the gear it needs.</p><p>When a gig is booked, its <strong>Gear</strong> tab fills from the packages sold: two products each needing a speaker need two. <strong>Add Gear from Packages</strong> adds anything new (after an add-on, say) without removing what you added by hand.</p></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_gear_music_s1_l2" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_gear_music" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Packing</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">12</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>Tick items off as they go in the van: "2 of 6 packed" at the top. Anything needing more than you own is flagged in red. The Gig Sheet prints the list with boxes to tick on the day.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/performers_elearning/static/img/gear_tab.png" alt="A gig's gear checklist" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>a gig's Gear tab, two items packed.</p></div></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_gear_music_s2" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_gear_music" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Music</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">22</field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_gear_music_s2_l1" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_gear_music" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">The client's lists</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">23</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>Clients fill in two lists from their order in the customer portal: <strong>Must play</strong> (with the moment, like First dance) and <strong>Do not play</strong>. They can change them until the gig starts.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/performers_elearning/static/img/portal_music.png" alt="The client's music lists in the portal" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>the client's view.</p></div><p>Both lists are on the gig's <strong>Music</strong> tab too, for you to edit.</p></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_gear_music_s2_l2" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_gear_music" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Song requests from guests</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">24</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>Every booked gig has a private song request page. <span class="oe-path">Print Song Card</span> on the Music tab prints a card with its QR code for the tables (the Gig Sheet ends with one too).</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/performers_elearning/static/img/song_request_phone.png" alt="The song request page on a phone" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>what a guest sees.</p></div><p>Requests close when the gig ends, and each phone can send a few at a time. On the Music tab, or in <span class="oe-path">Sales › Orders › Song Requests</span> during the gig, mark them <strong>Played</strong> or <strong>Skip</strong>; a request for a do-not-play song is shown in red.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/performers_elearning/static/img/music_tab.png" alt="A gig's Music tab" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>a gig's Music tab: the client's lists and guest requests.</p></div></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_gear_music_s2_l3" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_gear_music" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Songs to Get</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">25</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p><span class="oe-path">Sales › Orders › Songs to Get</span> lists the must-play songs and guest requests for upcoming gigs that you don't have yet. Mark each <strong>Got it</strong>, or <strong>Can't get</strong> with a note saying why: the client sees that note on their must-play list and can pick another song.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/performers_elearning/static/img/songs_to_get.png" alt="Songs to Get" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>songs still to get for an upcoming wedding.</p></div></div></field>
    </record>
