    <record id="channel_promotion" model="slide.channel">
        <field name="name">Getting Booked Again</field>
        <field name="channel_type">training</field>
        <field name="description" type="html"><p>List the gigs you play at other people's events, and give promoters a press kit page.</p></field>
        <field name="visibility">members</field>
        <field name="enroll">invite</field>
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="enroll_group_ids" eval="[(6, 0, [ref('sales_team.group_sale_salesman')])]" />
    </record>
    <record id="channel_promotion_s1" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_promotion" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Appearances</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">10</field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_promotion_s1_l1" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_promotion" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Gigs at other people's events</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">11</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>An event someone else runs, where you're performing, is an <strong>Appearance</strong>: tick it on the event. Your website lists it with your own events, with a badge ("Performing"), but nothing is sold or registered in Odoo.</p><p>On the <span class="oe-path">Appearance</span> tab: the host, how people get in (tickets sold by the host, registration with the host, free entry, or just more information), the host's link and the button's label, and the host's flyer and materials to show on the page.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/performers_elearning/static/img/appearance_form.png" alt="An event set up as an appearance" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>an appearance at a festival.</p></div><div class="oe-callout"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-bullhorn" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">Promote It</span><p>On a booked public gig, <strong>Promote It</strong> creates a draft appearance from the gig: add the host's link and flyer, then publish it.</p></div></div></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_promotion_s2" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_promotion" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Press kit</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">21</field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_promotion_s2_l1" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_promotion" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Your press kit page</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">22</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>Promoters, venues and journalists all ask for the same things. <span class="oe-path">Website › Site › Press Kit</span> puts them on one page, <code>/press-kit</code>: your bio, genres, where you're based, booking contacts, photos, mixes and videos, a technical rider and a Book button.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/performers_elearning/static/img/press_kit_form.png" alt="The press kit form" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>filling in the press kit.</p></div><p>Your upcoming events and appearances appear on it by themselves. Photos show at web size and download at full size, so they print well. Tick <strong>Published</strong> and add the page to your menu.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/performers_elearning/static/img/press_kit_page.png" alt="The press kit page" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>the published page, in the website's own colors.</p></div></div></field>
    </record>
